From e8b8e44f37f305d71ec493ecbc0430c87a8a79a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): 64 KiB chunked, %globaltimer-paced side-stream
 L2 prefetch

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (spark-ds41f-1107 0001..0761).

Rationale:
On GB10 (sm_121a, 273 GB/s LPDDR5X), cp.async.bulk.prefetch.L2.global.L2::cache_hint
honors chunk sizes up to 64 KiB (65536 bytes; 128 KiB and 1 MiB requests are ignored)
and feeds a finite hardware TMA prefetch FIFO. Launching grid * 128 threads (256 threads
at grid=2 on TP4, or 512 threads at grid=4 on TP3) that each issue unpaced 4 KiB
bulk-prefetch requests overflows the TMA prefetch FIFO (making grid=4 40-42 us/layer
slower than grid=2 even during zero-memory windows) and floods the memory controller
during concurrent window kernels.

Update both the TileLang L2 prefetch kernel (vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/tilelang/l2_prefetch.py)
and the CuTe DSL L2 prefetch kernel (vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/l2_prefetch.py) so a
single issuer thread (CTA 0, lane 0) walks the (ptr, bytes) segment table in 64 KiB
(65536-byte) bulk-prefetch chunks with an initial 128 KiB (2-chunk) burst followed by
200 ns %globaltimer pacing between subsequent chunks. Keep a separate _SLICE_BYTES = 4096
alignment granule in take_budget so all L2PrefetchPlan segment tables remain unchanged.

Quality implications:
None (cache-hint-only L2 prefetch; 100% bit-exact outputs across all decode and draft steps).

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_glm5next_tilelang_l2_prefetch.py
- pytest tests/models/test_glm5next_l2_prefetch_persist.py
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py
- pytest tests/models/kimi_k3/test_l2_prefetch.py

Upstream status:
Local SM121a GB10 hardware optimization.
